    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d991">

                <pb facs="0866" n="854" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.014G/471</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Knox</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-10-19">October 19, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: You will remember at the
                    Cabinet meeting Friday, the President suggested I get a clearance from your
                    Department on the matter of the Galápagos Islands.</p>
                <p>The suggestion made was that an arrangement be had under which a landing field
                    and an anchorage for flying boats be established there and paid for out of the
                    funds set up for that purpose.</p>
                <pb facs="0867" n="855" xml:id="pg855"/>
                <p>I shall be very glad to have your Department indicate whether it is agreeable to
                    you for these negotiations to be initiated.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank Knox</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
